ember fears returning to the hiking thread as "the guy who disappeared for four months and came back talking about the weather."\n- Member reports no bodily signals when with people and says it isn\'t that kind of thing.\n- Member keeps returning to a book at the storage unit their mother wanted them to read; she got to chapter nine and Member never did, and Member sat with it then put it back and kept working.\n- Member\'s reason the book is hard to open is that there would be nobody to tell about it, as their mother would have asked the next Sunday.\n- Member cut short their last call with their mother to watch a deploy, saying "Love you, gotta run," and keeps thinking about it.\n- Member says the issue is not processing the book with someone but that the last thing they said to their mother was about a deploy.\n- Member declined an exercise to talk to the moment, saying they just wanted to say it out loud to something.\n- Member said half the conversation felt like the counsellor guessing at them and stopped the session.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nI think I broke Marcus\'s house.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nI hear the weight in that statement. When you say "broke Marcus\'s house," do you mean something literal happened, or are you using that to describe how you’ve made him feel?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nA pipe burst in his utility room, so no, literal<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nWhen did it happen, and have you spoken to Marcus about it yet?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nWednesday night. Marcus knows, he was there<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nIt sounds like a stressful situation. Right now, are you more focused on the practical side (what needs to be done) or the emotional weight of it (guilt, worry, obligation)?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nPractical. Plumber, the insurance, repacking what got wet<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\nSince it\'s the practical side that\'s in focus, let me make sure I have the basics: Are you handling 