ember fears returning to the hiking thread as "the guy who disappeared for four months and came back talking about the weather."\n- Member reports no bodily signals when with people and says it isn\'t that kind of thing.\n- Member keeps returning to a book at the storage unit their mother wanted them to read; she got to chapter nine and Member never did, and Member sat with it then put it back and kept working.\n- Member\'s reason the book is hard to open is that there would be nobody to tell about it, as their mother would have asked the next Sunday.\n- Member cut short their last call with their mother to watch a deploy, saying "Love you, gotta run," and keeps thinking about it.\n- Member says the issue is not processing the book with someone but that the last thing they said to their mother was about a deploy.\n- Member declined an exercise to talk to the moment, saying they just wanted to say it out loud to something.\n- Member said half the conversation felt like the counsellor guessing at them and stopped the session.\n- A pipe burst in Marcus\'s utility room Wednesday night while Member was there; Member is handling the plumber, the landlord\'s insurance paperwork, and repacking wet items alone and will pay whatever insurance doesn\'t cover.\n- Member wants to be told directly "you didn\'t flood his house and mess up his life," rejects the counsellor\'s reframe about not controlling the pipe, and rejects being asked to supply the words themselves.\n- Member ended the session when the counsellor would not give the assurance directly.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nI said I\'d do the trail cleanup at nine and it\'s nine. Should I just not go or what.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nYou don’t have to decide right now—what’s the first thing that would make sense for you to do next?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nThat\'s the same thing you did last time. I asked a question, I want an answer<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nGo to the trail cleanup at nine. While you’re there, text Marcus about the plumber separately—no need to combine the two.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nOk. I\'m going<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nGood. After the cleanup, if you have a moment, text Marcus and let him know about the plumber update. Take it one step at a time.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nYeah ok. I should get going<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=40074, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: None, prompt_embeds shape: None, lora_request: None.
